# Waiz Media OS

When working in this repository:

1. Read [docs/SOURCE-OF-TRUTH.md](docs/SOURCE-OF-TRUTH.md) and [docs/_inventory/migration-backlog.md](docs/_inventory/migration-backlog.md) before converting or moving docs.
2. Use the **waiz-business-os** skill ([.claude/skills/waiz-business-os/SKILL.md](.claude/skills/waiz-business-os/SKILL.md)) for structure, templates, and gap analysis.
3. Use the **docx** skill when extracting from `.docx` in `source-docs/`. Use **xlsx** for spreadsheet wrappers.
4. Never edit `source-docs/waiz-drive-export/`. Output canonical Markdown under `docs/` only.
5. Check [docs/_inventory/duplicate-resolutions.md](docs/_inventory/duplicate-resolutions.md) before converting overlapping sources.
6. New docs: YAML frontmatter, kebab-case paths, `status: draft` until human approval.
7. After SOP or playbook updates in `docs/`, offer team Google Drive publish per [team-doc-publish](.claude/skills/team-doc-publish/SKILL.md). Published docs must match [WM Objection Categories](https://docs.google.com/document/d/19creUTdx5cTwWJVjdX3qPUMY40v1z379bCNoieY_Q5Y/edit) per [wm-team-doc-format-spec.md](docs/templates/wm-team-doc-format-spec.md). Repo is source of truth; Drive is one-way team output only.

